<article class="env-exercise" id="0AAQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AAQ">Exercise <span data-tag="0AAQ">111.57.4</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. Let $b : X \to \mathbf{A}^2_ k$ be the blow up of the affine plane in the origin. In other words, if $\mathbf{A}^2_ k = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k[x, y])$, then $X = \text{Proj}(\bigoplus _{n \geq 0} \mathfrak m^ n)$ where $\mathfrak m = (x, y) \subset k[x, y]$. Prove the following statements </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the scheme theoretic fibre $E$ of $b$ over the origin is isomorphic to $\mathbf{P}^1_ k$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$E$ is an effective Cartier divisor on $X$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the restriction of $\mathcal{O}_ X(-E)$ to $E$ is a line bundle of degree $1$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> (Recall that $\mathcal{O}_ X(-E)$ is the ideal sheaf of $E$ in $X$.) </p>
</article>